  "# SmartNutri AI: Privacy Notice (DRAFT)\n\n**Last updated:** [date]\n**Data Fiduciary:** [legal entity name], [registered address], India.\n\nSmartNutri AI (\"SmartNutri\", \"we\") helps you check whether a packaged food suits each member of your family, and track what they eat. This notice explains what personal data we process, why, where, for how long, and your rights under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (DPDP Act).\n\n**SmartNutri gives information, not medical advice.** It does not diagnose, treat, manage or cure any condition. Ask a qualified doctor or dietitian about your diet.\n\n## 1. What we collect\n\n| Category | Examples | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Account data | Email address or phone number, sign-in identifiers, preferred language | To sign you in and run your account |\n| Family profiles | Each member's name or nickname, relation, birth year, sex (optional), diet (veg, Jain and so on) | To give each member their own verdict |\n| **Health data** (only with your `health_data` consent) | Allergies, health conditions (for example diabetes or PCOS), goal, height, weight | To check products against each member's needs |\n| Food data | Barcodes you scan, products you add, label values you confirm, meals you log | To show verdicts, history and summaries |\n| Label photos | Photos of food labels you take | To read the label for you |\n| Voice questions | Short recordings of your questions and our spoken answers | To answer questions about a product |\n| Technical data | App version, device type, crash reports, coarse usage events | To keep the service working and secure |\n\nWe never collect a member's full date of birth, and we do not collect identity documents.\n\n## 2. Purposes and consent\n\nWe ask for separate consents, and you can withdraw each one at any time:\n\n- **`terms`:** to use the service under our Terms. This covers the core service: verdicts, scans, meal logs and **reading the label photos you take**. To read a label, we send the photo to an AI model. The photo holds no family or health data, and we remove its location and other hidden details (EXIF) first.\n- **`health_data`:** to save your family's health data (allergies, conditions, goal, height, weight). Verdicts use the health data you have saved; without it, they cannot take a member's allergies or conditions into account.\n- **`ai_processing`:** to send product data and member profiles, with names and IDs removed, to AI models that write explanations of a verdict and answer voice questions.\n\nVerdicts (`ok`, `caution`, `unknown`, `avoid`) are calculated by our own rules, never by an AI model. AI only reads labels and explains the result. [Lawyer: confirm that label reading can rest on `terms` as part of the core service, see ADR 0018 ruling G1.]\n\n## 3. Where your data is processed\n\n- Your account and family data are stored in India: Supabase in Mumbai, and our servers on Google Cloud in Mumbai.\n- When an AI model receives member health information, we use a model processed in India, and we remove names, emails and IDs before sending.\n- Label photos contain no health data. The AI model that reads them may process them outside India. [Confirm the extraction model's processing region before launch.]\n- Crash reports (Sentry) and usage analytics (PostHog) may be processed outside India. **They never receive health data**, member names, emails or the content of your requests. Analytics use a hashed (one-way) identifier.\n\n## 4. How long we keep data\n\n| Data | Kept for |\n|---|---|\n| Label photos | **30 days**, then deleted automatically. We keep them without location or other hidden details (EXIF): both apps remove these before upload, and our server removes them again when it reads the photo. The values you confirmed stay with the product. |\n| Voice recordings | Your recording is never stored. Our spoken answers are deleted after **24 hours**. Transcripts are never stored. |\n| Account, family profiles, health data, meal logs | Until you delete them or delete your account |\n| Consent records | For as long as we need to show what you agreed to and when |\n| Record that an account was deleted | **7 days** after deletion: only the account's internal ID and the time, so that a sign-in from before the deletion cannot bring the account back |\n| Crash reports | Up to 90 days, in the provider's retention settings |\n\n## 5. Your rights\n\n- **Access and correction.** You can see and edit your family profiles in the app.\n- **Withdraw consent.** Use Profile → Privacy and consent. Withdrawal is as easy as giving consent. After you withdraw, we stop the processing that needed that consent: for example, we will not save new health details without `health_data`, and we will not use AI without `ai_processing`. Your stored profiles stay, and allergies and conditions already saved are still checked so a product is never shown as fine for someone with a saved allergy. To erase them, delete the member or your account (see below). [Lawyer: confirm against DPDP s. 8(7); see ADR 0018 and its ruling G1 amendment.]\n- **Erasure.** Profile → Delete account permanently deletes your account, family profiles, health data, scans, meal logs, label photos, voice answers and consent records. It also removes your sign-in. Products you added to the shared catalogue stay, with no link to you. You can also ask us by email: [privacy email].\n- **Grievance redressal.** Our Grievance Officer is [name], [email], [phone], [address]. We reply within [7] days and resolve within [30] days. If you are not satisfied, you may complain to the Data Protection Board of India.\n- **Nominate.** You may nominate another person to exercise these rights if you die or become incapacitated. Contact the Grievance Officer.\n\n## 6. Children and other family members\n\nSmartNutri accounts are for adults (18+). An adult may add profiles for children and elderly parents and manage them. By adding a member, you confirm that you are their parent, lawful guardian, or authorised to manage their data. We do not track children, show them targeted ads or profile their behaviour. [Lawyer: confirm verifiable parental consent under DPDP s. 9 and the Rules.]\n\n## 7. Sharing\n\n**We do not sell your data and we show no ads.** We share data only with the service providers that run SmartNutri for us (data processors under contract):\n\n- Supabase: database, storage and sign-in\n- Google Cloud: hosting\n- CallMissed: AI models, speech, and WhatsApp sign-in codes\n- Sentry: crash reports\n- PostHog: usage analytics\n\nWe also share data where Indian law requires it.\n\n## 8. Open Food Facts\n\nSome product information comes from Open Food Facts (openfoodfacts.org), available under the Open Database License (ODbL). We never send your personal data to Open Food Facts.\n\n## 9. Security\n\nData is encrypted in transit (HTTPS) and at rest. Access is limited per account by row-level security. Label photos and voice answers are in private storage and reached only through short-lived links. We will tell you and the Data Protection Board about a personal data breach as the law requires.\n\n## 10. Changes\n\nIf we change this notice in a way that affects your consent, we show the new version in the app and ask you again before continuing.\n\n## Contact\n\n[privacy email] · Grievance Officer: [details above]\n";
